# Verb-parity conformance profile [PROFILE:PROFILE-VERB-PARITY]

> ⛔ THE POINT OF THIS FILE. The parity test must read its verbs FROM A PROFILE, because
> transcribing them into a Python literal is the exact move that produced the defect it
> exists to catch: `control.expected.json` hand-picked two members of a table the engine
> enumerates, both worked, and the suite was green while four other verbs minted nothing.
> Registration here, assertion in the test, and NOTHING in between that re-states the list.
>
> ⛔ BOOTSTRAPPING INVARIANT (`factlattice/profile.py::_assert_core_only_parse`). A profile
> is parsed with CORE notation only — it cannot use the vocabulary it registers. There is
> therefore no `## Relationships` section here and no relationship-bearing property.

## [PROFILE-DOMAIN] Domain identity

- domain-id: cf.parity
- domain-name: Conformance — verb-surface parity fixture
- domain-version: 1.0
- namespaces: cf.parity

## Registered relationship verbs

> BARE verbs. Registration is what makes `[A] VERB [B]` a recognised triple — and, since
> [FL-VERB-PARITY], what makes `- verb: [B]` mint the same edge. One registration, two
> surfaces, by derivation rather than by a second table someone has to remember.

### [EDGETYPE-USES] A consumes or applies B

- edge-type: USES
- tier: domain
- definition: A consumes or applies B. The single-word shape, and the verb whose property key `uses` was measured minting zero edges across 13 authored lines.

### [EDGETYPE-UPHOLDS] A preserves invariant B

- edge-type: UPHOLDS
- tier: domain
- definition: A preserves the invariant B. The verb whose property key `upholds` was measured minting zero edges across 14 authored lines.

### [EDGETYPE-DOCUMENTS] A is the provenance record for B

- edge-type: DOCUMENTS
- tier: domain
- definition: A is the provenance record for B. Its property key `documents` reads as an ordinary English plural, which is exactly why an author writes it and exactly why nobody noticed it minted nothing.

### [EDGETYPE-REALIZES] A makes design B real

- edge-type: REALIZES
- tier: domain
- definition: A makes the design B real.

### [EDGETYPE-APPLIES-AT-PHASE] A applies at phase B

- edge-type: APPLIES_AT_PHASE
- tier: domain
- definition: The MULTI-WORD UPPER_SNAKE shape, present so the kebab derivation (`APPLIES_AT_PHASE` -> `applies-at-phase`) is checked rather than assumed.
